{
  "id": "v-eagle-task-50-ubuntu",
  "snapshot": "eagle-7.7.0",
  "instruction": "look at `vias.brd` in the EAGLE board editor. The board contains 8 vias, all drilled to `0.3 mm`. Shrink the three vias listed in `targets.txt` to `0.2 mm` drill and save the result as `resized.brd`.\n\nRequirements:\n- `resized.brd` remains a well-formed EAGLE 7.x board XML file.\n- It still has exactly 8 `<via>` elements.\n- The three vias at the coordinates listed in `targets.txt` have `drill=\"0.2\"`.\n- The other five vias still have `drill=\"0.3\"`.\n- Element, signal, and wire counts match the starter exactly; do not delete or reroute anything.\n\nOnly resize vias listed in `targets.txt`.",
  "source": "https://community.element14.com/products/eagle/f/eagle-user-support-english/5464/changing-drill-size-for-all-vias",
  "config": [
    {
      "type": "upload_file",
      "parameters": {
        "files": [
          {
            "local_path": "task-50/init_file/targets.txt",
            "path": "/home/user/Desktop/targets.txt"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "upload_file",
      "parameters": {
        "files": [
          {
            "local_path": "task-50/init_file/vias.brd",
